DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sqrt((sqrt((1/(x)))))");
$fun_1 = Formula("(((x^2))^2)^4");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(-infinity, 11) U (-infinity, 11) U (-infinity, 11)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(-infinity, 12) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 12)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((-infinity, 12)))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("((-infinity, 18] U (-infinity, 18]) U ((-infinity, 18]) U {-8, 0, 1, 2, 6}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-8, 0, 1, 2, 6} U {-8, 0, 1, 2, 6}");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("{-8, 0, 1, 2, 6} U {-8, 0, 1, 2, 6}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`10+2-8-12`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(-8.),width=>4}
---

[`19+16-1+18*5`] is equal to [_____]{Real(124.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, 0, 1, 2, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 18\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x < 17\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B \cup B) \cup (B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 11\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x < 12\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cap B \cap (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -3, 10, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 3, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 5, 9, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, 9, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-3, 10, 7>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, 3, 4>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 9, 10>") x Compute("<7, 3, 4>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 10, 7>") x Compute("<5, 9, 10>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -1, 9, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 2, 9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 2, 9>") x Compute("<-1, 9, 3>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, 2, 9>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-1, 9, 3>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, 9, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
